# Commit review gate

In Claude Code, `scripts/hooks/review-gate.mjs` refuses any `git commit` whose content `/review` and
`/ponytail:ponytail-review` did not both see byte for byte; an edit after a review needs a fresh review. Generated paths
(`sync:maintainer-agents` output, `.cursor/commands/`, `packages/blit386/docs/_api-history.json`) are exempt. Cursor has
no such hook, but the rule is the same: review after your last edit, then commit.

Claude: `.claude/rules/commit-review-gate.md` (full content).
